-- title:
--   An A-algebra field of characteristic p receives A through 𝔽ₚ
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a natural number $M \neq 0$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ for the set $\{p\}$, and let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \operatorname{LaurentSeries} L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. to the $L$-subfield of $\operatorname{LaurentSeries} L$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise map induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (Gamma1 (M * p))` of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain equipped with an $L$-algebra structure making $L$ its fraction field, such that the image of $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and some element of $A$ maps to $\zeta$, together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with that of $L$; let $j \in K$ be an element, assumed nonzero, whose underlying Laurent series is the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) (the series $q^{-1}$ times the rational-coefficient $j$-numerator power series) under the coefficientwise map. Finally let $k$ be a field of characteristic $p$ with an $A$-algebra structure. Then there is a ring homomorphism $r \colon A \to \mathbb{Z}/p$ whose composition with the canonical map $\mathbb{Z}/p \to k$ equals the structure map $A \to k$.
--
--   The assertion is that the structure map of any characteristic-$p$ field over the ring of integers $A$ of $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)$ localised at $p$ factors through the residue field $\mathbb{F}_p$, so that such a field is canonically an $\mathbb{F}_p$-algebra compatibly with its $A$-algebra structure. It is used to install the $\mathbb{F}_p$-algebra structures required by the statements about models over $\mathbb{F}_p$ of the modular curve $X_1(Mp)$ and its special fibre, in the analysis of Frobenius on components.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_exists_ringHom_zmod_castHom_comp_eq_algebraMap_of_isCyclotomicExtension.lean

